# Hobbitify Working Memory

## Repository shape
- This repo uses `react-app/` as the frontend (React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind).
- Backend code is in `backend/`.

## Where to make changes
- Default all product/UI work to `react-app/`.

## API and data expectations
- Backend request payload should use `{ input: string }` for modern flows.
- Skill data is hierarchical and may arrive as either a JSON string or an object; parse defensively.
- Preserve root-skill detection via parent/child relationships when rendering trees.

## React app conventions
- TypeScript first: avoid `any` unless unavoidable.
- Reuse existing helpers in `src/utils/` and types in `src/types/`.
- Follow current UI style tokens/classes from Tailwind config (`bg-*`, `text-*`, `accent-*`, `border-*`).
- Keep components focused and prefer small helper functions over inline complex logic.

## Quality checks
- For `react-app/` edits, run:
  - `npm run lint`
  - `npm run build` for substantial changes
- Do not commit generated secrets or `.env` values.

## Collaboration defaults
- If asked to "update UI", assume `react-app/` unless explicitly told otherwise.
- Keep changes scoped, explain assumptions, and list any follow-up verification steps.
